  "scope": "First bounded actual nested-execution slice: certified total construction, exact source equations, occurrence-rank correctness and connected source-count cases. Actual run<=F remains next mandatory continuation.",
  "private_construction": "Valid-rank worker receives the actual already measured entry length and its equality proof. It returns Measured {a // a\u2208xs} Nat. Only membership, actual chunk-count descent and partition lengths justify subsequent recursion; no recursive rank correctness or selection cost law is assumed. The public Option boundary evaluates length once and uses the cached value for its invalid guard.",
  "public_parameterization": "Resources.Selection.selectRunWith (groupSize cutoff : Nat) (hd : 2\u2264groupSize) (hc : 1\u2264cutoff) (k : Nat) (xs : List \u03b1); book selectRun specializes5/20. Arbitrary duplicates, no Inhabited/Nodup.",
  "source_path": "Exactly one recursive pivot selection at cached index (ceil(n/d)-1)/2; partition executes once; lower length always at recursive source branch; equal length only after failed left test; return pivot directly in equal branch; at most one strict recursive child. Every recursive entry obtains its own actual length observation.",
  "explicit_optional_extension": "Invalid k\u2265n returns none with one selector entry plus one length observation, so cost n+2, including empty cost2. This is disclosed Lean totalization, not a book out-of-range value/cost assertion.",
  "cases_reference_method": "Independent Python implementations of recursive insertion, sort, lookup, chop, median-map and nested selection computed these finite targets before new Lean source. Exact valid book targets match the frozen selection-proof-plan table. This is preparation, not Lean validation.",
